(KEY-16 — `Create` also starts a directory creation (`mkdir(2)`); the
 article is optional, `called` is required.
 Also covers: KEY-17 (`Remove`/`Delete` a directory).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox KEY-16.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   directories made
   directories gone
)
Create a directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-16".
On error print "mkdir failed".
Create directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-16-second".
On error print "mkdir without the article failed".
Print "directories made".
Remove the directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-16".
On error print "rmdir failed".
Delete the directory "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-16-second".
On error print "delete failed".
Print "directories gone".
